WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.840
The new Mortal Kombat film is filled with easter&nbsp;
eggs, both in what is shown, and what characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.880
say. Here are the lines in Mortal Kombat that&nbsp;
have a deeper meaning than first meets the eye.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.920
One of the central narrative arcs in&nbsp;
Mortal Kombat is the rivalry between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.400
Hanzo Hasashi who becomes Scorpion&nbsp;
and Bi-Han also known as Sub-Zero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.240
The film opens with Bi-Han killing&nbsp;
Hanzo's entire clan, family, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:37.280
then the man himself. Before he does, Bi-Han says:
"...the Shirai Ryu, have been exterminated by me."&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.760
With this line, the movie fast-tracks the&nbsp;
backstory of Scorpion and Sub-Zero's clans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.440
and their long-simmering blood-feud. The Shirai&nbsp;
Ryu clan itself is actually an offshoot from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.080
Sub-Zero's, called the Lin Kuei, which began&nbsp;
when a member defected and started amassing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.400
their own followers. The Lin Kuei did not&nbsp;
take this defection lightly and made it their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.000
mission to wipe the new Shirai Ryu clan out of&nbsp;
existence. Hence, Sub-Zero's bloody mission.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.000
Cole Young, the once successful MMA&nbsp;
fighter who now can't win a match,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.160
is first approached about the Mortal Kombat&nbsp;
tournament by Major Jax Briggs after an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:18.080
unsuccessful fight. Even though we just saw Cole&nbsp;
take a pretty decisive loss, Jax refers to him as:&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.560
"The man that took the belt from Eddie Tobias."
The line is delivered in a manner that is clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:26.960
meant to make it seem like Eddie Tobias&nbsp;
is a formidable MMA fighter. The fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:31.440
Cole once robbed him of a title means he was&nbsp;
much more successful in his younger years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:36.400
But that's beside the point. The name itself is&nbsp;
also meant to be a loving reference to Ed Boon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.800
and John Tobias, the developers credited&nbsp;
with creating the first Mortal Kombat game.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:48.080
Another deep concept that gets a cursory mention&nbsp;
in the movie is that of the Elder Gods. When Shang&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.200
Tsung is preparing to assassinate the Earthrealm&nbsp;
warriors, Mileena pushes back by asking:&nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.920
"What of Lord Raiden? If he discovers we're&nbsp;
breaking rules set in stone by the Elder Gods..."&nbsp;

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.400
The Elder Gods are beings whose job is to&nbsp;
ensure balance among the many realms by using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.680
non-interventionist methods. Despite Mileena's&nbsp;
fear of them retaliating against Shang Tsung for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.680
breaking the rules they've set, the Elder&nbsp;
Gods themselves are not all-powerful.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.640
Similar to the pantheon of Greek deities, the&nbsp;
Elder Gods are significantly more human in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.440
way they operate than other interpretations&nbsp;
of a divine and omniscient being. The Elder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.680
Gods Shinnok and Cetrion have even been&nbsp;
playable characters in the game series.&nbsp;

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.840
Considering the Amulet of Shinnok appeared&nbsp;
as an Easter egg moment in the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.240
we’re curious to see how much of a role the&nbsp;
Elder Gods play in the film series going forward.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.560
When the Earthrealm warriors find Raiden's&nbsp;
temple, Cole and Kano are quickly put on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.440
an intense training regime in order to build&nbsp;
their skills and unlock their arcana abilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:50.080
As Kung Lao begins to put the would-be defenders&nbsp;
of the realm through their paces, he says:&nbsp;

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.240
"All you can do now is test your might."
That line is pretty straightforward in the context&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.720
of the movie, but it's also a sly reference&nbsp;
to the first Mortal Kombat. Between fights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.800
players would occasionally be tasked with&nbsp;
competing in a button-mashing minigame called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.800
"Test Your Might," wherein their character had&nbsp;
to punch through blocks of wood and other strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:12.240
materials to score points. The nonchalant callback&nbsp;
in the 2021 movie seems like an Easter egg left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.840
specifically for players whose love of the&nbsp;
games goes all the way back to the first.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.160
Although Liu Kang has been featured as the&nbsp;
protagonist for many of the games and movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.640
in the Mortal Kombat universe, he plays&nbsp;
more of a supporting role in the 2021 film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.720
He still gets the opportunity to shine some&nbsp;
light on his backstory, though. While speaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:36.080
with Cole between training sessions, he reveals:
"Unlike Kung Lao, I was just a worthless stray.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.640
For reasons beyond my ken, master Bo'&nbsp;
Rai Cho found me half-dead in a gutter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.320
and brought me to the Wu Shi Academy."
Like many of the franchise's characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:48.720
Liu Kang's backstory got fleshed out&nbsp;
considerably as the series went on.&nbsp;

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:56.320
"I die in the Koliseum? You on a rooftop, fighting&nbsp;
Lord Raiden? Our future, Liu Kang. It is insane."&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:02.560
The 2002 game Mortal Kombat: Deadly Alliance&nbsp;
introduced the character Bo' Rai Cho,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:07.120
the Outworld martial arts grandmaster who turned&nbsp;
his back on his home-realm to train Earthrealm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:12.720
warriors like Liu Kang and Kung Lao. Bo' Rai&nbsp;
Cho's status as an Outworlder on the side of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.200
Earthrealm makes him a significant character&nbsp;
in the general lore of the games, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.920
considering Liu Kang secured several Earthrealm&nbsp;
victories in the Mortal Kombat tournaments.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:28.160
While many characters in the Mortal Kombat series&nbsp;
have fascinating histories and storylines, there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:33.520
are only a handful that have real significance&nbsp;
to the broader arc of the story. The 2021 film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:38.880
smartly brings in several that are less important&nbsp;
as fatality fodder, one of those being Kabal.&nbsp;

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.760
In the movie, Kabal is introduced as an assassin&nbsp;
working for Shang Tsung and an associate of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:48.480
Kano's. He even says of his old frenemy:
"He's the reason I live in an iron lung."&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:52.880
Kabal's distinct mask and breathing apparatus&nbsp;
have been a hallmark of his character since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.120
he was first introduced in Mortal Kombat 3.&nbsp;
However, while the movie implies that Kano&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.840
caused the injuries that put Kabal in his iron&nbsp;
lung, in the games, the story is a bit different.&nbsp;

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:07.200
In 2009's Mortal Kombat, a reboot that retells the&nbsp;
story of the first three games, Kabal is a police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.680
officer who sustains grievous injuries during&nbsp;
Outworld's invasion of Earthrealm. He's found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.160
by Kano, who fits him with his respirator that&nbsp;
allows him to breathe despite the damage to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:21.680
lungs. So, in the games, Kano quite literally puts&nbsp;
Kabal in his iron lung, but only to save his life.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:27.520
Although Raiden's warriors feel outmatched&nbsp;
by Shang Tsung's collection of assassins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:30.800
the former ends up pretty much wiping&nbsp;
the floor with the latter. That doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:34.960
seem to bother Shang Tsung too much, though.&nbsp;
Shortly before the credits roll, he announces:&nbsp;

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:40.080
"Today you have killed my warriors and you think&nbsp;
you have won. But death is only another portal."&nbsp;

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:43.840
The Mortal Kombat games have featured&nbsp;
several narrative arcs wherein previously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.880
slain characters rise from the dead. In Mortal&nbsp;
Kombat 3, Shang Tsung helps resurrect Sindel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:54.320
the wife of Outworld Emperor Shao Kahn. Similarly,&nbsp;
the tenth installment of the series saw multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:59.200
dead characters return as mind-controlled versions&nbsp;
of their former selves known as Revenants.&nbsp;

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:03.280
The evil sorcerer also menaces the&nbsp;
Earthrealm warriors with a warning:&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.880
"Next time I see you I will not&nbsp;
bring fighters, I will bring armies."&nbsp;

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:10.880
While the first two games tell stories that&nbsp;
are relatively contained to the tournaments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:16.560
Mortal Kombat 3 features an all-out war. The plot&nbsp;
of the game sees Shao Khan enlisting Shang Tsung&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:20.080
to pull some trickery that ends with&nbsp;
the emperor invading Earthrealm with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.520
armies of Outworld warriors.
If or when the Outworld invasion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:28.080
happens in the films, Shang Tsung's threat&nbsp;
to come back with armies is not an idle one.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:33.360
The original Mortal Kombat had a&nbsp;
relatively small roster of characters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:37.600
There were only seven playable fighters and&nbsp;
three special bosses included in the game.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.840
All ten of those characters made an&nbsp;
appearance in the 2021 film except for one:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.960
The vain martial artist&nbsp;
and movie star Johnny Cage.&nbsp;

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.800
Cage doesn't make a physical appearance in&nbsp;
the first movie, but based on the ending,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.360
fans will be seeing him if there's a sequel.&nbsp;
After defeating Shang Tsung's forces, we see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:57.840
Cole in the locker room of the MMA arena when&nbsp;
he's approached by his fight booker. He declines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.640
the man's offer to appear in a matchup, saying&nbsp;
that he's off to Hollywood. The man replies:&nbsp;

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:06.320
"Hollywood? What the hell's in Hollywood?"
Fans of the series likely knew the answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:10.400
to that question as soon as it was asked.&nbsp;
But to hammer home reference, the camera&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:14.400
lingers on a poster for a movie starring&nbsp;
Johnny Cage right before the credits roll.&nbsp;

